=== Follow-up: multi-source VJP-cache regression (real DynamicCache storage) ===
HEAD: 2a5ddd372b7b2fe64a8e853553178fbde2cdc6d4 (parent checkpoint, untouched)

Scope: documentation + focused regression only. No computation-graph change.
The suspected leafness bug was reviewed and disproved on a real 3-layer model:
DynamicCache.update returns concatenated storage, so every returned source
(including the earliest selected layer) is a non-leaf intermediate; both
returned cache tensors are valid autograd.grad inputs with finite nonzero VJPs.
Per the parent re-scope we DO NOT alter the graph for leafness and DO NOT
assert is_leaf.

Change:
- src/steering_lite/variants/vjp_cache.py: concise comment in
  ValueGradientCache.update explaining why only min(selected) incoming value is
  detached (seeds the graph; later selected values remain graph-connected
  intermediates accepted by autograd.grad) and why later values must NOT be
  detached (would sever earlier-layer forward influence).
- tests/test_pipeline.py: test_vjp_cache_two_source_real_storage_hybrid_exclusion
  - Qwen3.5 hybrid, 5 layers: [full, full, linear, full, linear]
  - selected sources (0,1,3), target 4; layer 2 is a non-selected recurrent
    (linear-attention) layer sitting between sources and target.
  - proves both returned cache tensors are actual DynamicLayer storage
    (cache.sources[l] is cache.layers[l].values), finite nonzero VJPs of shape
    (batch, kv_heads, seq, head_dim), and selected/non-selected exclusion
    (linear layers 2/4 never appear in sources). No is_leaf assertion.

